{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791622847,"nonce":"IdJzbH7iZzvsURF+pL9LfYHE430=","title":"Animations stall until the mouse moves; overlays, tabs and drags look wrong","message":"Reported from running cn_demo (not reproduced headlessly): dropdowns and popovers show with no enter or exit animation, dialogs, drawers and sheets feel too quick, tabs just switch, toast exits are janky, the slider and resizable panels are jumpy during a drag, and animations do not move until the mouse moves.\n\nChecked headlessly, all fine at 071b439e: a class rule's animation starts (on a built node and on one that arrives in a subtree rebuild), follows its keyframes, and lands on a painted node (the windowed loop's redraw gate); the theme's motion tokens resolve into the cn stylesheet (duration-fast 150ms, duration-normal 200ms with the default tokens, 180ms in Hybrid); the exported ease-out curve evaluates correctly (about 0.57 at a quarter of the time, 0.84 at half); a tab panel and a router page play their exit when a render state is driven in the runner's frame order.\n\nNot checked: the windowed loop itself. 'Not moving until I move the mouse' means no redraw term stays true while an animation is active, so the loop parks. The terms are in blinc_app windowed.rs (any_redraw_signal: needs_animation_redraw, needs_motion_redraw, needs_overlay_redraw, css_needs_redraw, overlay_css_needs_redraw); most are gated on painted_node_ids / painted_stable_ids. Only three commits this week touch the runner, paint, motion, overlays, animation or theme: 7c3f82e0 (drain), 793cfcb0 (display: none paint), 3ae37876 (svg tint). Needed: RUST_LOG=blinc_app=debug output ('frame pacing: which signal is live') while a dropdown opens and stalls, and the last commit or date where animations worked.\n\nMotion tokens: CSS-driven animations (dropdown, popover, context menu, hover card, nav menu) use var(--duration-*) and var(--ease-*). Dialog, drawer and sheet take their curve from ease_sheet but hard-code the duration (dialog 200/150ms, drawer 250ms, sheet 300/225ms); tabs fade 250ms and router transitions 200-300ms are hard-coded too. A 150ms ease-out (cubic-bezier 0,0,0.2,1) is 84% done at half time, so it reads as quicker than its length.\n\nSlider: a drag queues a subtree rebuild at hover, press, first drag and release (it is still a Stateful\u003cSliderThumbState\u003e); mid-drag events queue none and the drag math is linear. Resizable not looked at yet.","files":null}]}